### **About Me**

I am a Computer Science graduate with a strong interest in applying machine learning and data-driven methodologies to real-world challenges, 
particularly in the domains of healthcare and drug discovery. My academic and research work is centered on developing computational models 
that integrate advanced algorithms with domain-specific knowledge to generate meaningful and actionable insights.I have hands-on experience 
in building predictive models using techniques such as Random Forest, XGBoost, and Support Vector Machines. Additionally, I have explored 
explainable artificial intelligence approaches, including SHAP and LIME, to enhance the interpretability and reliability of model outcomes. 
My research interests also include Quantitative Structure–Activity Relationship (QSAR) modeling, clustering techniques, and molecular docking 
studies for identifying and validating potential drug candidates.I am proficient in Python and experienced in executing end-to-end machine 
learning pipelines, encompassing data collection, preprocessing, feature engineering, model development, evaluation, and deployment. I am 
particularly interested in developing scalable and reproducible solutions using modern technologies such as containerization and cloud-based 
platforms. I am committed to continuous learning and collaborative research, with a focus on interdisciplinary applications that bridge computing 
with biological and medical sciences. My long-term goal is to contribute to impactful research and develop innovative solutions that can be 
translated into practical applications in healthcare and related fields.
